<body>
    <h1>Use Cases and Request Form Requirements</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <div class=3D"contentLayout2">
 <div class=3D"columnLayout two-equal" data-layout=3D"two-equal">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <p>The followings are the user profile scenarios, rules and requirement=
s to cover all current use cases for client access requests. Only CX access=
 and R2 access are considered; the linked system access, e.g. SZ, NetRep an=
d OSS are not in focus.&nbsp;</p>
    <p><br></p>
   </div>
  </div>
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <p>
     <style type=3D"text/css">/*<![CDATA[*/
div.rbtoc1788898048098 {padding: 0px;}
div.rbtoc1788898048098 ul {margin-left: 0px;}
div.rbtoc1788898048098 li {margin-left: 0px;padding-left: 0px;}

/*]]>*/</style></p>
    <div class=3D"toc-macro rbtoc1788898048098">
     <ul class=3D"toc-indentation">
      <li><a href=3D"#UseCasesandRequestFormRequirements-Assumption">Assump=
tion</a></li>
      <li><a href=3D"#UseCasesandRequestFormRequirements-Dependency">Depend=
ency</a></li>
      <li><a href=3D"#UseCasesandRequestFormRequirements-UserProfileScenari=
os">User Profile Scenarios</a></li>
      <li><a href=3D"#UseCasesandRequestFormRequirements-UIRules">UI Rules<=
/a></li>
      <li><a href=3D"#UseCasesandRequestFormRequirements-AccessRequestForm"=
>Access Request Form</a></li>
     </ul>
    </div>
    <p></p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <h1 id=3D"UseCasesandRequestFormRequirements-Assumption">Assumption</h1=
>
    <ul>
     <li data-uuid=3D"42e25089-555b-4451-8917-e1454690dc2b">Employee Access=
 SSO has been launched=20
      <ul>
       <li data-uuid=3D"a6130639-7f44-46b9-af9c-34f40390a997">Employees use=
r accounts (primary) are not in-scoped in UAR</li>
      </ul></li>
    </ul>
    <p><br></p>
    <h1 id=3D"UseCasesandRequestFormRequirements-Dependency">Dependency</h1=
>
    <ul>
     <li data-uuid=3D"5b79ca90-557d-442f-a2c1-d08cc7a2c89b">SZ SSO and app =
link integration depend on the launch of UAR=20
      <ul>
       <li data-uuid=3D"6537e9fb-7923-4de3-8dbc-4488e5414970">Must provide =
a way for clients to choose apps/services offered on SZ, which are now inte=
grated and accessed via Compass</li>
      </ul></li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"f8ab68c9-5524-4612-9d27-7b5e70b88e77"><span style=3D"=
letter-spacing: 0.0px;">R1/R2 decommissioning</span>
      <ul>
       <li data-uuid=3D"2cd89e69-331c-4ae2-b3d9-dee957c6c382"><span style=
=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">Must provide a way for clients to choose the Le=
gacy Compass features (aka R2 features) before sunsetting the Legacy Securi=
ty Steward feature (aka Manage Firm Users)&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span></li>
      </ul></li>
    </ul>
    <p><br></p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <h1 id=3D"UseCasesandRequestFormRequirements-UserProfileScenarios">User=
 Profile Scenarios</h1>
    <p>These are scenarios by the type of users who have unique access need=
s.</p>
    <div class=3D"table-wrap">
     <table class=3D"relative-table wrapped confluenceTable" data-snooker-c=
ol-series=3D"numbers" data-snooker-locked-cols=3D"0" style=3D"width: 92.252=
9%;">
      <colgroup>
       <col style=3D"width: 5.00264%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 9.49482%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 9.49482%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 12.4595%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 26.2537%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 37.2945%;">
      </colgroup>
      <tbody>
       <tr>
        <th class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTh" contenteditable=3D"false=
" data-mce-resize=3D"false" scope=3D"col"><br></th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Product Version</th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Target release</th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Scenario</th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Profile settings</th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Requirements</th>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd" contenteditable=3D"false=
" data-mce-resize=3D"false">1</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Initial load</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p><span class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-current">2=
026 Q4</span></p>
         </div></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">User migration&nbsp;</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Data plotting</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"e89bad2a-b553-4462-813c-28b8a2161510">All curren=
t client user data must be plotted to the new model</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"f3138559-1525-42e4-9ae7-bacd1ec4330d">The user a=
ccess of all current clients are maintainable via UAR</li>
          <ul>
           <li data-uuid=3D"905cf833-b11f-4e3a-a392-dfbdac3d1d0d">In specif=
ic, the access data can be rendered in the request form for user monitoring=
 and modification request&nbsp;</li>
          </ul>
         </ul>
         <p><strong>Additional data requirement:&nbsp;</strong><span style=
=3D"letter-spacing: 0.0px;">load all NetRep Ids for NBIN clients **discuss =
with Radhika</span></p>
         <p>**Solution requirement for one-time data update</p></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd" contenteditable=3D"false=
" data-mce-resize=3D"false">2</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Happy path</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p><span class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-current">2=
026 Q4</span></p>
         </div></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Create New users</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>CX Id =E2=86=92 R2 Id =E2=86=92 SZ Id =E2=86=92 NetRep id (1 to=
 1)</p>
         <p>Identical data access</p>
         <p>Identical feature access categorization&nbsp;</p></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Able to handle the new user requests of the 1-to-1 user scenari=
o&nbsp;</p>
         <p>Q: How to identify who can use this form and screen out those w=
ho cannot?</p>
         <p>- Won't happen to new user request. Not allowed.</p>
         <p>**This user type covers 90% of user population.</p></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd" contenteditable=3D"false=
" data-mce-resize=3D"false">3</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Happy path</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p><span class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-current">2=
026 Q4</span></p>
         </div></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Modification</p>
         <p>(add/remove access)</p></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">User accounts created from UAR</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Able to handle the user modification requests for those who are=
 created by UAR</p>
         <p>Q: How to identify who can use this form and screen out those w=
ho cannot?</p>
         <p>- Decision point: Should the solution triage the users, or by o=
peration means? E.g. a procedure to handle <strong>non-standard users </str=
ong>non-digitally.</p>
         <p>- After the initial load, we can identify those who cannot fit =
in this process, we can design an <strong>alternate flow (how?) </strong>fo=
r them. **Handle in the user modification request (epic)</p></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd" contenteditable=3D"false=
" data-mce-resize=3D"false">4</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p style=3D"margin: 10.0px 0.0px 0.0px;"><span style=3D"letter-spa=
cing: 0.0px;">Happy path</span></p></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p><span class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-current">2=
026 Q4</span></p>
         </div></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">User deactivation &amp; reactivation</td=
>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Any client user accounts</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Able to capture user deactivation requests for operations to di=
sable user accounts for the user across systems</p>
         <p>- Same as above</p></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd" contenteditable=3D"false=
" data-mce-resize=3D"false">5</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Next</p></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p><span class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-current">2=
026 Q4</span></p>
         </div></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Parent firm users in SZ</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>1 CX Id to multiple SZ Ids</p>
         <p>(non-standard users)</p></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Must confirm it is supported through CX-SZ SSO integration (to =
be launched by 2026 Q4)</p>
         <p>Q: How to identify which SZ Id the request is about? Especially=
 after UAMA integration, SZ Id is not shared to clients -- legacy users kno=
w their SZ Ids</p>
         <p>- To be handled by the&nbsp;<strong style=3D"letter-spacing: 0.=
0px;">alternate flow (how?) mentioned above</strong></p></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd" contenteditable=3D"false=
" data-mce-resize=3D"false">6</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Next&nbsp;</p></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p><span class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-current">2=
026 Q4</span></p>
          <p><br></p>
         </div></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Traders / Operation people</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>No CX Id but NetRep Id only</p>
         <p>No CX Id, no NetRep Id but OSS Id</p></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Business decision: Is it mandatory to create a CX Id for these =
users? - no</p>
         <p>If no, how UAR handle user access request access (new/change) f=
or their NetRep Id without a CX Id reference? **Handle in the off-platform =
epic.&nbsp;</p>
         <p>**Key takeaway:</p>
         <p>- Netrep Id and OSS Id must be searchable via the user monitori=
ng.&nbsp;</p>
         <p>- For one-time initial load, load all NetRep Ids for NBIN clien=
ts **discuss with Radhika</p>
         <p>- when someone requests a new user, NetRep access only, we don'=
t need to create the CX Id but create the Person account only - get aligned=
 with JP.</p></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd" contenteditable=3D"false=
" data-mce-resize=3D"false">7</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Later</p>
         <p>(Workaround available)</p></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p><span class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-moved">202=
7 Q1 / Q2</span></p>
         </div></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Parent firm users in R2</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>1 CX id to multiple R2 Ids</p>
         <p><br></p></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Dependency: Multi-firm user feature (2027 Q1)</p>
         <p>Workaround (Recommended approach): request a second CX id to ma=
intain 1-to-1</p></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd" contenteditable=3D"false=
" data-mce-resize=3D"false">8</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Later</p>
         <p>(Workaround available)</p></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p><span class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-moved">202=
7 Q1 / Q2</span></p>
         </div></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">PM sub-advisors</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>1. The PM sub-advisor works for a firm which is our client</p>
         <p>2. The PM sub-advisor is a third-party not associated to any of=
 our clients</p></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Dependency: Multi-firm user feature (2027 Q1)</p>
         <p>Workaround (Recommended approach): request a second CX id to ma=
intain 1-to-1:</p>
         <ol>
          <li data-uuid=3D"d41fc6e9-3f8b-49a0-bcce-ae385369ac0b">They have =
their home firm CX Id, plus a CX Id for each firm they sub-advise</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"1aeca427-28c0-4714-b53b-bd5e8c926e12">Their CX I=
d is under the firm they are sub-advising to, one Id per sub-advising firm<=
/li>
         </ol></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd" contenteditable=3D"false=
" data-mce-resize=3D"false">9</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">??</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">??</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd"><strong>Cross-firm RR code assignments i=
n SZ or NetRep</strong></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Most likely happen to parent firm users or PM sub-advisors,</p>
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"5b46beab-16d0-4cb7-805e-ec2a22fba421">1 CX Id to=
 1 SZ Id and 1 CX Id to 1 NetRep Id</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"418c1b5e-13c5-488a-af7f-a80dc38933db">The SZ Id =
and/or NetRep Id is assigned to RR codes across multiple firms</li>
         </ul>
         <p>There is no concept of firm ranges or any RR code edits in SZ a=
nd NetRep.</p></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Dependency: Multi-firm user feature (2027 Q1)</p>
         <p><br></p>
         <p>Q: How to request RR codes outside of their firm range to be ad=
ded to their SZ Id or NetRep Id?</p></td>
       </tr>
      </tbody>
     </table>
    </div>
    <p><br></p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <h1 id=3D"UseCasesandRequestFormRequirements-UIRules">UI Rules</h1>
    <p>These rules are agnostic to the request form structure.</p>
    <div class=3D"table-wrap">
     <table class=3D"wrapped relative-table confluenceTable" data-snooker-c=
ol-series=3D"numbers" data-snooker-locked-cols=3D"0" style=3D"width: 91.926=
2%;">
      <colgroup>
       <col style=3D"width: 7.98435%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 12.4408%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 21.8738%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 27.5908%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 30.1103%;">
      </colgroup>
      <tbody>
       <tr>
        <th class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTh" contenteditable=3D"false=
" data-mce-resize=3D"false" scope=3D"col"><br></th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Eligible Firm / Special Ca=
se</th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Client User Story</th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">NBIN Requirement</th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Importance (Critical/High/=
Medium)</th>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd" contenteditable=3D"false=
" data-mce-resize=3D"false">1</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Client IDP firms</p>
         <p>(e.g. IAVM)</p></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">As a FSS, I want to provide the <strong>=
External ID</strong> for my users when requesting a new CX Id, so that they=
 can single signon CX through the company portal.</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>External ID and IDP source (e.g. indall) must be populated for =
SSO firm users when creating their CX Id</p>
         <p>Current state: User admin UI cannot handle it but the bulk SSO =
user creation flow can.</p></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p><span class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-current">H=
IGH</span></p>
          <p>Workaround: Continue with the current flow to onboard new SSO =
users.</p>
         </div></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd" contenteditable=3D"false=
" data-mce-resize=3D"false">2</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">PM sub-advising firms</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">As a FSS, I want to add/update the <stro=
ng>PM sub-advisor RR codes</strong> to the user accounts for my firm's PM s=
ub-advisors, so that they can access the sub-advising accounts and action a=
ccordingly.</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>The PM sub-advisor RR codes are used in <strong>R2 only</strong=
> because CX doesn't support PM sub-advisor use cases yet. Some R2 use case=
s:</p>
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"cfbfed14-6238-4eb8-890f-a78a37b6f02d">My Account=
</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"92e72729-fd22-4587-b74a-966ee2d5c941">Trade Advi=
ce File Upload</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"49fe50c3-12af-420f-b294-54a90bfd5e73">Mutual Fun=
d File Upload</li>
         </ul>
         <p><u>Data validation</u>: The input RR codes must be validated be=
fore being persisted.&nbsp;</p>
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"3357f164-b583-43b1-bc5e-47fe14efd9ab">Current ru=
les used in R2: The RR code is valid and belongs to a PM firm</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"b6747083-b65b-4901-ac0f-eabe8bd4fe24">We should =
add a rule that the RR code belongs to the firm that submits the request</l=
i>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p><span class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-error">CRI=
TICAL</span></p>
          <p>There is no workaround. Unable to manage the attribute via UAR=
 means that the legacy security steward feature cannot be decommissioned.</=
p>
          <p><br></p>
         </div></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd" contenteditable=3D"false=
" data-mce-resize=3D"false">3</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Self-account opening firms (Broadridge a=
ccess)</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">As a FSS, I want to be able to assign an=
 <strong>Onboarding profile and Division (if applicable)</strong>&nbsp;for =
my users so that they can perform their account opening responsibilities.</=
td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">The selectable options of onboarding pro=
files and divisions must be driven by the respective firm settings.</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p><span class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-error">CRI=
TICAL</span></p>
          <p>There is no workaround. Unable to manage the attribute via UAR=
 means that the legacy security steward feature cannot be decommissioned.</=
p>
          <p>**Key takeaways:&nbsp;</p>
          <p>- Should be mapped by the CX access controls when requesting C=
ore: Onboarding</p>
          <p>**Check with Radhika</p>
         </div></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd" contenteditable=3D"false=
" data-mce-resize=3D"false">4</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Broadridge firm settings</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">As a NBIN Support team, I want to config=
ure the <strong>Broadridge firm settings</strong> for all firms, so that th=
e firm users can be set up with the appropriate onboarding profile and divi=
sion by their firm.</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Firm settings for Onboarding apps availa=
ble</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p><span class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-current">H=
IGH</span></p>
          <p>The firm settings do not change often. The Firm Access mainten=
ance can be easily go offline as an alternative.</p>
          <p>**Key takeaways:</p>
          <p>- Are the firm specific controls necessary?<span style=3D"lett=
er-spacing: 0.0px;">&nbsp;</span></p>
          <p>&nbsp;**Check with Caroline</p>
          <p><br></p>
         </div></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd" contenteditable=3D"false=
" data-mce-resize=3D"false">5</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Internal feature filter</p>
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"55627e39-0675-4390-a118-69da43f2439b">Features w=
hich are for NBIN-use only.</li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">As a NBIN Product team, I want <strong>i=
nternal features </strong>to be absent from UAR, so that our clients cannot=
 be bothered with the options which are not applicable to them.</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Must be able to identify "internal features" in the catalogs.</=
p>
         <p>UAR (the form and downstream processes) must be able to filter =
out internal features.</p>
         <p>Known issues:</p>
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"79042d12-a28d-4f43-a31d-452681f0e4be">Cannot sup=
port Notifications on internal features - TBC</li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p><span class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-error">CRI=
TICAL</span></p>
          <p>In case internal features are assigned to clients by mistake, =
the consequences will be unacceptable, for example, access error, inappropr=
iate feature/data exposure. Even if the features are just shown up on the a=
ccess request form, it may invite unnecessary inquiries from clients.&nbsp;=
</p>
          <p><strong>**Requirements: Onboard all features, which are on or =
linked to CX, to feature registry, but not showing internal features to ext=
ernal user request election.</strong></p>
         </div></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd" contenteditable=3D"false=
" data-mce-resize=3D"false">6</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Feature state filter</p>
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"b3697011-6ae4-4102-ba4e-76e06ec921cd">Pre-releas=
ed features</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"b430779d-c720-4459-88e1-3328a37ed9b1">Active fea=
tures</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"013ede33-8d06-4a15-8d13-88e2a792cf73">Deprecated=
 features</li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">As a NBIN Product team, I want to releas=
e active features<strong> </strong>for our clients to select through UAR by=
 manipulating the feature state, so that our clients cannot be exposed to p=
re-released features or deprecated features.</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"93f161ce-c406-4c26-8534-1e3b596dd015">Only activ=
e features must be available in UAR</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"eed71b51-a960-458e-92d3-c5efc7e22a63">Pre-releas=
ed and deprecated features must not be available</li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p><span class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-error">CRI=
TICAL</span></p>
          <p>Feature state indicates whether the feature is launched and re=
ady for clients or not. Exposing pre-released or deprecated features for ac=
cess request will result in system risk.</p>
         </div></td>
       </tr>
      </tbody>
     </table>
    </div>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <h1 id=3D"UseCasesandRequestFormRequirements-AccessRequestForm">Access =
Request Form</h1>
    <p>These are product requirements and stakeholder feedback in regard to=
 the Form, in particular the Feature Access section.</p>
    <div class=3D"table-wrap">
     <table class=3D"wrapped relative-table confluenceTable" data-snooker-c=
ol-series=3D"numbers" data-snooker-locked-cols=3D"0" style=3D"width: 85.275=
2%;">
      <colgroup>
       <col style=3D"width: 3.11088%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 14.7296%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 48.3187%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 30.7292%;">
       <col style=3D"width: 3.1116%;">
      </colgroup>
      <tbody>
       <tr>
        <th class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTh" contenteditable=3D"false=
" data-mce-resize=3D"false" scope=3D"col"><br></th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Topic</th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Requirement</th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Rationale</th>
        <th scope=3D"col" class=3D"confluenceTh">Priority</th>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd" contenteditable=3D"false=
" data-mce-resize=3D"false">1</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Core services</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">At least one of the four core services m=
ust be selected</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Platform UI would fail to render the lef=
t-nav if there's no accessible module</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p><span class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-error">CRI=
TICAL</span></p>
         </div></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd" contenteditable=3D"false=
" data-mce-resize=3D"false">2</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Ineligible combinations</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Some options must not be available to be chosen at the same tim=
e.&nbsp;</p>
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"71e5a667-0c7e-4ad5-9540-e22560361e2f">Example, i=
f Account Opening is "Control", cannot choose Manage Order Mgmt. There are =
around 31.</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"d25d03fc-7019-4ce7-8244-212f7a0bb6ff">Details to=
 follow - Radhika's list</li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>The specific permutation does not exist in any user package.</p=
>
         <p>We are not adding new user packages.</p></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p><span class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-error">CRI=
TICAL</span></p>
         </div></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd" contenteditable=3D"false=
" data-mce-resize=3D"false">3</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">User Access Management options</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Must not be presented for selection (e.g=
. manage firm, manage user)</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">FSS onboarding should follow the BAU pro=
cess (TBC)</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p><span class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-error">CRI=
TICAL</span></p>
         </div></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd" contenteditable=3D"false=
" data-mce-resize=3D"false">4</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Firm settings filter</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Remove features which are not applicable=
 or opted out by the firm</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Avoid confusion</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p><span class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-error">CRI=
TICAL</span></p>
         </div></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd" contenteditable=3D"false=
" data-mce-resize=3D"false">5</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Association between module and optional =
entitlement</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Flag error if an optional entitlement is selected while the mod=
ule it bundles under is unselected, and vice versa.</p></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"a059e128-0f94-4255-9121-1e443f47afe5">Validate c=
lient selection upfront to prevent unresolvable scenarios</li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p><span class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-error">CRI=
TICAL</span></p>
         </div></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd" contenteditable=3D"false=
" data-mce-resize=3D"false">6</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Dependency&nbsp;</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Flag error if dependency is not met</p>
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"d9e3070b-63ed-4f51-b221-18dfafeb4a9b">Example-1,=
 Manage Order is selected but no optional entitlement (EQ, MF, OP) is selec=
ted</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"538da379-ea5a-448e-955d-c615f120dbb8">Example-2,=
 Manage MF Basket is selected but Manage MF Order is not selected&nbsp;</li=
>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"fd5b5dc1-043c-48a5-982a-a05f29fcb573">Validate c=
lient selection upfront to prevent unresolvable scenarios</li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p><span class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-error">CRI=
TICAL</span></p>
         </div></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd" contenteditable=3D"false=
" data-mce-resize=3D"false">7</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Default form settings</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <ol>
          <li data-uuid=3D"3617c6b8-c92b-4de8-9b2f-e9cb64df1b6e">Everything=
 is none</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"d7c173e0-9b96-4b55-9e21-06208d07e582">When View =
is chosen for Client Inquiry and Insights (first option), turn on "View" in=
 everything below</li>
         </ol></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"d956be14-1b06-42a6-bac7-fe0ae01ec2c2">Streamline=
 the user experience</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"5c611dd5-a049-4343-ae49-388450c5ef78">Prevent in=
eligible options to be chosen</li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p><span class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-current">H=
IGH</span></p>
         </div></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd" contenteditable=3D"false=
" data-mce-resize=3D"false">8</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Form update while editing</p>
         <p>(User experience suggestion)</p></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Must not present to clients ineligible options based on what ha=
ve been selected</p>
         <p>e.g. eliminate options from the form</p>
         <p><br></p></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"322fa409-16cb-497f-a748-8e570d143e71">Streamline=
 the user experience</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"2066bdb4-83a2-46bc-96c0-21a2d476737a">Prevent in=
eligible options to be chosen</li>
         </ul>
         <p>Alternatively, clients may choose all options and be told, at t=
he end, that their selections are not eligible, which is not a good user ex=
perience.</p></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p><span class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-current">H=
IGH</span></p>
         </div></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd" contenteditable=3D"false=
" data-mce-resize=3D"false">9</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Presentation suggestion</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Q: How to tell the optional entitlements are associated with wh=
ich features/modules listed?</p>
         <p>1. Only present features when the right level of access is sele=
cted</p>
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"4307b525-35f2-4c1e-ac74-6d0e263a67e4">e.g. "GIC"=
 is only visible if Manage is selected on Orders Mgmt, not View Orders Mgmt=
</li>
         </ul>
         <p>2. Allow clients to see clearly the dependencies between module=
 and optional entitlements, and make their selection accordingly</p>
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"5c041f16-b378-4c3f-b9ae-9cea3203e122">Example, "=
Approve option application" is applicable FBO only, but there's no associat=
ion to the listed modules (Account opening, estate, ...)</li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"b22af07d-fd0d-40f0-9197-c4ac86d4d3fe">Streamline=
 the user experience</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"9538e98a-9b83-46a7-80d6-81b31666f563">Prevent in=
eligible options to be chosen</li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p><span class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-current">H=
IGH</span></p>
         </div></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd" contenteditable=3D"false=
" data-mce-resize=3D"false">10</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Access control tier</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Q: How to ensure clients choose the access level just fit their=
 needs, not over?</p>
         <p>Allow clients to distinguish the "extra" features from the view=
 tier to the manage tier, so on so far, so that they can make the decision =
on the right level of access controls they need.</p>
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"fa68eb06-a03c-4cac-b669-a562f00e5519">Example, w=
hen a higher level is selected, it should be clear that clients would get "=
everything from the next lower level, plus..."</li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"386146d9-c896-41e9-b659-5d0658b4ecb9">Prevent ov=
er-provisioning</li>
          <li data-uuid=3D"595d4434-c672-4e7a-8fa9-9833a882a536">Usability<=
/li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p><span class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-current">H=
IGH</span></p>
         </div></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd" contenteditable=3D"false=
" data-mce-resize=3D"false">11</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Inconsistency in module definition</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>The feature registry (xls) and the implementation are not an ex=
act match in module definition. There is a risk the form selection cannot b=
e mapped to the correct Compass user access.&nbsp;</p>
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"dcf326c3-d0dd-4098-87ab-8f932cbe4c86">Example, O=
rders (GIC) is implemented as a module, not as an optional entitlement unde=
r manage orders. The form presentation is not wrong but to transfer the sel=
ection to access update may request an exception handling, unlikely the EQ =
order, MF order selection.</li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"6d5263dd-2858-4d03-aa1a-58f3521e00cd">Risk of op=
erational friction</li>
         </ul>
         <p><br></p></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p><span class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-current">H=
IGH</span></p>
         </div></td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"numberingColumn confluenceTd" contenteditable=3D"false=
" data-mce-resize=3D"false">12</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <p>Undo or reset selections</p>
         <p>(User experience suggestion)</p></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Able to undo the last changes&nbsp;</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <ul>
          <li data-uuid=3D"4a58a4d1-02f9-4f39-b5c8-d524c2c1d1e8">Usability<=
/li>
         </ul></td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">
         <div class=3D"content-wrapper">
          <p><span class=3D"status-macro aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-current">H=
IGH</span></p>
         </div></td>
       </tr>
      </tbody>
     </table>
    </div>
    <p><br></p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
</div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
------=_Part_2959_1750794621.1788898048119--
